1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,520
This session is about the duties and responsibilities

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,740
of directors and we'll also look at some

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,500
of the provisions of the Communist and Allied

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,640
Matters Act as well as the Nigerian Code

5
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:12,160
of Corporate Governance and the outline of my

6
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:15,440
presentation at this session is the duties and

7
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:18,780
responsibilities of directors, the highlights of the Code

8
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:21,240
of Corporate Governance as well as guidelines on

9
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:24,180
corporate governance, the role of the board and

10
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:26,920
how the board can achieve effectiveness as well

11
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:29,560
as identifying in effectiveness.

12
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,080
So as we start I think it's important

13
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:35,820
to define some of the terms we'll be

14
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:36,380
using here.

15
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:40,280
Essentially according to the law there's really no

16
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,400
difference between executive and non-executive directors and

17
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:46,020
so it would be redundant to speak about

18
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:48,760
executive and non-executive directors from the liability

19
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:50,280
or responsibility perspective.

20
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,460
Executive directors have day-to-day duties, non

21
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:58,560
-executive directors on the other hand periodically attend

22
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,660
meetings and have responsible oversight and strategy.

23
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,160
However, if you are looking at the liability

24
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,180
of the board as a whole there is

25
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:09,380
no distinction between both categories of directors.

26
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,960
So we're going to the specific officers of

27
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:15,920
the board i.e. the executive, non-executive

28
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,960
and the independent non-executive directors.

29
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,880
So I'll start with the executive directors.

30
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:24,140
They have day-to-day responsibilities like I

31
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:27,700
said earlier on to run the organisation and

32
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:32,200
they typically have contracts of employment that define

33
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,140
these roles.

34
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:36,740
They're also hired based on their knowledge, experience

35
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:40,000
and expertise and they're held accountable for those

36
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,160
particular responsibilities.

37
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:45,920
They have a responsibility to ensure that the

38
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:49,060
amount of information available to them is also

39
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:50,860
available to the entire board.

40
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:54,620
There's usually an asymmetry of information between the

41
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:57,700
two categories of directors because like I said

42
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:00,860
the executive directors have a day-to-day

43
00:02:00,860 --> 00:02:05,640
responsibility and they have specific roles regarding the

44
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,440
operations of the business and as such they

45
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:11,760
have real-time information about the business.

46
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:15,560
That real-time information is not available to

47
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:18,580
the people who consider to be outside directors

48
00:02:18,580 --> 00:02:21,960
or non-executive directors and as such the

49
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:24,540
responsibility lies on the executives to make sure

50
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:27,400
that all of the information they have is

51
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,600
made available to the non-executives so that

52
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:32,500
they can take decisions that are robust based

53
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,320
on all the facts.

54
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:37,740
However, it doesn't absolve the non-executive directors

55
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:40,320
to say that oh we acted based on

56
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,760
only the information that we had.

57
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,520
They also have a responsibility to demand for

58
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:47,240
the information that they require in the form

59
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,720
and manner that they require such information as

60
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,640
well as the frequency of such information.

61
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:56,720
The other category of directors of course is

62
00:02:56,720 --> 00:03:00,240
the managing director who is also an executive

63
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:00,880
director.

64
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,740
He or she is appointed based on the

65
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:06,860
skills that he or she has and essentially

66
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:10,560
that person has oversight of the entire management

67
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,020
team.

68
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:13,980
The organisations where you have just the one

69
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:16,780
executive director who typically is a managing director

70
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:20,580
and for larger organisations you have him leading

71
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:22,220
the other executive directors.

72
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:28,180
The third category of directors are the non

73
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:31,340
-executive directors and they are appointed from outside

74
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,000
of the company.

75
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:35,300
So they could be shareholder representatives, they could,

76
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,900
I mean they don't necessarily have their own

77
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:39,760
shares but a lot of the time typically

78
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:43,040
they are shareholder representatives and as such they

79
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:47,140
bring they expect to bring independent judgement based

80
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:49,760
on their own experience from other things that

81
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,600
they're involved with.

82
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:54,060
Typically one expects that they're involved in either

83
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:56,320
their own businesses or their own careers or

84
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:59,240
professions and they bring the robustness of that

85
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,680
experience onto the board.
